WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:05.260
No one expected the final trailer for the
Harry Potter prequel Fantastic Beasts: The

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:09.290
Crimes of Grindelwald to tell them anything
they didn't already know from watching previously

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:11.170
released teasers and TV spots.

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:16.150
But when Warner Bros. dropped the last piece
of promotional footage on September 25, minds

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.150
were blown.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.150
Why?

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:22.050
Because it features a brief clip of a woman
named Nagini turning into a snake.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:26.000
And that has opened a huge can of worms for
Harry Potter fans, leading Harry Potter author

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.000
J.K.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.070
Rowling to issue a public defense of the film.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:33.850
In the original Harry Potter series, Nagini
was a gigantic sinister snake who served as

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:39.140
the evil lord Voldemort's companion and assistant,
while also acting as a Horcrux, one of the

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.690
vessels for a portion of Voldemort's soul.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:46.550
Nagini was eventually slain by Neville Longbottom,
opening the way for Voldemort's final defeat.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:51.670
So the revelation that Nagini was once a human
woman that can turn into a snake - or possibly

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:55.860
a snake that turns into a woman - is definitely
a shocker for fans.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.980
But the surprise hasn't been all that welcomed
by everyone.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:03.910
Both longtime and casual fans of the franchise
have a number of concerns, perhaps most importantly

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:08.900
over the choice to cast South Korean actress
- and Marvel Universe veteran - Claudia Kim

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:09.950
in the role.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:14.189
Twitter user Jen Moulton started the firestorm
when she tagged Rowling in tweet that read

00:01:14.189 --> 00:01:15.189
in part,

00:01:15.189 --> 00:01:19.320
"Listen [...] we get it, you didn't include
enough representation when you wrote the books.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.700
But suddenly making Nagini into a Korean woman
is garbage.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.850
Representation as an afterthought for more
woke points is not good representation."

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:32.219
Other Twitter users piled on, with one decrying
the decision to cast one of the two actors

00:01:32.219 --> 00:01:35.170
of color in the Fantastic Beasts franchise
as a, quote,

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:38.340
"literal object owned by a white man inspired
by Nazis."

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:42.350
And others voiced concerns that the casting
choice bore echoes of old stereotypes, such

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:47.240
as those associating Asian people with snakes,
as well as the Dragon Lady cliché.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:51.130
Rowling didn't take the criticism lying down,
responding to the original attack with a tweet

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:52.130
that said,

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:56.610
"The Naga are snake-like mythical creatures
of Indonesian mythology, hence the name 'Nagini,'

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:01.200
They are sometimes depicted as winged, sometimes
as half-human, half-snake.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:06.469
Indonesia comprises a few hundred ethnic groups,
including Javanese, Chinese and Betawi.

00:02:06.469 --> 00:02:07.630
Have a lovely day."

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:11.730
She later added that she has been holding
onto the secret of Nagini's true nature for

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.370
"around twenty years."

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:17.800
That revelation seemed to actually spark even
more anger from another subsection of fans

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:22.010
who complain about Rowling's history of revealing
- or changing - details of the Harry Potter

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:24.720
universe years after the series wrapped up.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.980
Most famously, three months after the final
book came out in 2007, she announced that

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:32.180
Dumbledore was gay, and had been in love with
Grindlewald.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:36.010
Many applauded Rowling for the announcement,
but some felt she was trying to have her cake

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:41.150
and eat it too by pandering to LGBTQ fans
without truly taking the perceived risk of

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:44.819
actually portraying Dumbledore as gay in either
the books or films.

00:02:44.819 --> 00:02:49.720
The Dumbledore controversy gained new energy
in January 2018, when director David Yates

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:54.120
revealed that Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes
of Grindelwald won't make it "explicitly"

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.050
clear that Dumbledore, played by Jude Law,
is gay - despite the purported love of his

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:00.390
life being at the center of the sequel's story.

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:05.190
Instead, there seem to be just vague hints
for hardcore Harry Potter fans to decipher.

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:08.239
"Dumbledore why can't you go?"

00:03:08.239 --> 00:03:11.290
"I can't move against Grindelwald.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.290
It has to be you."

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:17.670
The Nagini and Dumbledore controversies are
just the latest PR hits for Fantastic Beasts:

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:21.610
The Crimes of Grindelwald, which has faced
intense scrutiny from the moment it was revealed

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:26.060
in November, 2017 that Johnny Depp was set
to return to the role of Grindelwald from

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:30.750
2016's Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find
Them despite highly publicized allegations

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:34.510
that he had assaulted his ex-wife Amber Heard
prior to their divorce.

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:38.600
It remains to be seen whether any of these
controversies will affect how Fantastic Beasts:

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:42.140
The Crimes of Grindelwald performs at the
box office when it arrives in theaters on

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:48.440
November 16, 2018, but one thing is for sure:
even if the film isn't a must-watch for everyone,

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:48.940
J.K.

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.020
Rowling's twitter feed definitely is.

